    <item>
      <title>The case for AI degrowth</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-026-02617-y</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Human Behaviour, Published online: 19 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-026-02617-y"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41562-026-02617-y&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Artificial intelligence (AI), as it currently unfolds, is incompatible with a sustainable transformation of the economy, which arguably requires degrowth. AI is the growth paradigm reborn — built on enclosed commons, powered by fossil energy, and driven by a competitive logic that makes precaution structurally impossible. Limits to AI growth are not technophobia; they are our best chance for a liveable future for all.</content:encoded>
      <dc:title>The case for AI degrowth</dc:title>
      <dc:creator>Matthias Schmelzer</dc:creator>
