    <item>
      <title>Motor abstraction training generalizes to the refinement of specific movement patterns</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-026-02597-z</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Human Behaviour, Published online: 19 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-026-02597-z"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41562-026-02597-z&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Practicing unfamiliar characters in rotated orientations improved upright writing as much as direct practice, showing that the motor system learns by abstracting a movement’s structure, not just its details.</content:encoded>
